{"severity":"error","file":"errors/realtime_mixed_1.march","start_line":20,"start_col":2,"end_line":22,"end_col":5,"message":"The function `step` takes `Tagged(_, Realtime)` but also takes `Cap(IO)`.\nRealtime functions cannot hold `Cap(IO)` — allocation, IO, and panic are excluded from realtime contexts.\nhint: remove `Cap(IO)`","code":"realtime_mixed","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/realtime_mixed_1.march","start_line":20,"start_col":52,"end_line":20,"end_col":59,"message":"`step` takes a `Cap(IO)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks.\nhelp: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `step` may use, give it a `needs` clause.","code":"cap_param_retired","fix":{"kind":"multi","edits":[{"kind":"replace","start_line":20,"start_col":43,"end_line":20,"end_col":59,"text":""}],"applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
